**[ASSUMPTION]** The RESULT interval is not a marginal interval over front definitions. If `DEPENDENCE family=frac` (and `smooth`, `winsor`, `combined_extreme`) is small, the luminous profile is nearly rigid and the speed is not an artifact of the half-maximum choice. If it is large, the profile is changing shape and a single front speed is definition-dependent; `WIDTH` and `CURVATURE` say how.

**[ASSUMPTION]** Classical SEs are too small when `DW_ROUGH` is far from 0. In that case prefer the printed `block_bootstrap` / `newey_west` limits as the uncertainty statement, and treat `ci95_*` as conditional on independent errors.

**[INFERENCE]** A negative `speed_mm_s` means the half-max contour moved opposite the predeclared body direction; that is reported, not repaired.

